            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Section\u202f2.01 of the Compact preserves the application of state water law, allowing each state to administer water rights in accordance with its own laws, subject to water availability under the Compact."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. O'Connell",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "65ce80bc475305c4194168ad7121e63e3ac2be6cf60e641e50f9b9f700fd5c8c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-65ce80bc4753-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. O'Connell, the legal question is whether a state law that conflicts with the Compact\u2019s allocation is preempted by the Compact."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "65ce80bc475305c4194168ad7121e63e3ac2be6cf60e641e50f9b9f700fd5c8c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-65ce80bc4753-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked whether a mechanism exists to enforce such preemption, suggesting none is in place."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "65ce80bc475305c4194168ad7121e63e3ac2be6cf60e641e50f9b9f700fd5c8c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-65ce80bc4753-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, justice Kagan questioned Ms. O'Connell\u2019s view, indicating uncertainty about accepting that argument."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "65ce80bc475305c4194168ad7121e63e3ac2be6cf60e641e50f9b9f700fd5c8c",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-65ce80bc4753-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia repeatedly asked \u201cWhere is this?\u201d highlighting concerns about locating the relevant authority."
      }
